              "officialWholeSourceCredit": false,
              "sourceContext": "NI KC Chemie SekII2022, Makromoleküle und Nanostrukturen, printed page32: polymer types, molecular structure/property explanation and selected polymer functionality. NI KC printed page50 A6 also lists the possible alternative teaching unit „Vom Kautschuk zum High-Tech-Reifen“.",
              "sourceLimit": "Synthetic-rubber production from a supplied monomer, vulcanisation and detailed4955 P transfer are SkillPilot extensions; not named universal NI official duties. The page50 named rubber context is a possible alternative, not a universal duty or proof of full synthetic-rubber/vulcanisation coverage or a persisted learner choice.",
              "rationale": "Retain the already authored LK elastomer example and acquire chain mobility and covalent crosslinking before its one-card conformational recall. Preserve the existing whole goal and all original HE provenance.",
              "existingRouteConsequence": "The unchanged4955→7f→0278 hard-prior route may add NI jurisdiction to7f(copolymers) and0278(PLA). Both have GK/LK tags and are already direct targets in BOTH de-ni-gym-chemistry-gk and de-ni-gym-chemistry-lk. A jurisdiction-only fixed point can therefore activate both existing course targets;4955 itself and recall d3 remain present only in the NI-LK raw view. These whole two goals/current P are deliberate SkillPilot extensions in both course targets, not official whole-source credit, a learner choice or universal necessary chemistry for rubber.",
              "authorRationale": "tmp/chemie-m7-resumed-20261016/NI4955-own-acquisition-compiler-input-author-successor-v1/FIRST.whole4955-NI-own-acquisition-and-source-limits.AUTHOR.frozen.json",
